AsyncTask.execute(Params...) is deprecated as of Android 11 (API 30) because AsyncTask encourages tightly-coupled, lifecycle-unsafe background work on the main-thread–adjacent scope, makes cancellation/error handling difficult, and can easily leak Activities. Google recommends coroutines, WorkManager, or other threading primitives (Executor/Handler/Thread) instead.

Two compatible alternatives for API 30 and later

1) Keep SSH, replace AsyncTask with Kotlin coroutines + a background Dispatcher (or Java Executor) and a modern SSH client (e.g., JSch/SSHJ). This preserves your current Raspberry Pi workflow.

Kotlin coroutine example (AndroidX Lifecycle):

// build.gradle (app)
// implementation 'org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-coroutines-android:1.7.3'
// implementation 'com.hierynomus:sshj:0.38.0' // or JSch if you prefer

class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {
    private lateinit var btnUp: Button
    private lateinit var btnDown: Button
    private lateinit var txtAddress: EditText

    // Example SSH params
    private val sshUser = "pi"
    private val sshPassword = "your-strong-password" // Prefer keys; see notes below
    private var wifiModuleIp = "192.168.1.100"
    private var wifiModulePort = 22

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)

        btnUp = findViewById(R.id.btnUp)
        btnDown = findViewById(R.id.btnDown)
        txtAddress = findViewById(R.id.ipAddress)

        btnUp.setOnClickListener { executeRemoteCommand("python /path/to/script.py --direction up") }
        btnDown.setOnClickListener { executeRemoteCommand("python /path/to/script.py --direction down") }
    }

    private fun executeRemoteCommand(command: String) {
        // Optionally read IP from UI
        wifiModuleIp = txtAddress.text?.toString()?.ifBlank { wifiModuleIp } ?: wifiModuleIp

        lifecycleScope.launch {
            val result = withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
                runCatching { sshExec(wifiModuleIp, wifiModulePort, sshUser, sshPassword, command) }
            }
            result.onSuccess { output ->
                Toast.makeText(this@MainActivity, "OK: $output", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show()
            }.onFailure { e ->
                Toast.makeText(this@MainActivity, "Error: ${e.message}", Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show()
            }
        }
    }
}

// Simple SSH via SSHJ (Java/Kotlin)
fun sshExec(host: String, port: Int, user: String, password: String, command: String): String {
    val client = net.schmizz.sshj.SSHClient()
    client.addHostKeyVerifier(net.schmizz.sshj.transport.verification.PromiscuousVerifier()) // For dev only; use real host key verification in prod
    client.connect(host, port)
    try {
        client.authPassword(user, password)
        client.startSession().use { session ->
            val cmd = session.exec(command)
            val stdout = cmd.inputStream.bufferedReader().readText()
            val stderr = cmd.errorStream.bufferedReader().readText()
            cmd.join()
            val exit = cmd.exitStatus ?: -1
            if (exit != 0) throw RuntimeException("Remote error ($exit): $stderr")
            return stdout
        }
    } finally {
        client.disconnect()
        client.close()
    }
}

Java (no coroutines) with ExecutorService:

// Replace AsyncTask with a single-threaded executor
private final ExecutorService exec = Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();

btnUp.setOnClickListener(v -> exec.submit(() -> {
    try {
        String out = sshExec("192.168.1.100", 22, "pi", "password", "python /path/to/script.py --direction up");
        runOnUiThread(() -> Toast.makeText(this, "OK: " + out, Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show());
    } catch (Exception e) {
        runOnUiThread(() -> Toast.makeText(this, "Error: " + e.getMessage(), Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show());
    }
}));

2) Replace SSH with a small HTTP endpoint on the Raspberry Pi and call it using OkHttp/Retrofit/WorkManager. This avoids SSH and AsyncTask entirely.

Minimal Flask service on Pi:

# pip install flask
from flask import Flask, request, jsonify
import subprocess, sys
app = Flask(__name__)

SCRIPT_PATH = "/path/to/script.py"
TOKEN = "change-me"  # Move to env var in production

@app.post('/action')
def action():
    if request.headers.get('X-Auth-Token') != TOKEN:
        return jsonify({'error': 'unauthorized'}), 401
    action = (request.json or {}).get('action')
    if action not in { 'up', 'down' }:
        return jsonify({'error': 'invalid action'}), 400
    cmd = [sys.executable, SCRIPT_PATH, '--direction', action]
    p = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return jsonify({'ok': p.returncode == 0, 'stdout': p.stdout, 'stderr': p.stderr}), (200 if p.returncode == 0 else 400)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=8080)

Android (Kotlin + OkHttp) caller:

// implementation("com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp:4.12.0")

lifecycleScope.launch {
    withContext(Dispatchers.IO) {
        val body = "{" + "\"action\":\"up\"" + "}"
        val req = okhttp3.Request.Builder()
            .url("http://$wifiModuleIp:8080/action")
            .addHeader("X-Auth-Token", "change-me")
            .post(okhttp3.RequestBody.create(okhttp3.MediaType.parse("application/json"), body))
            .build()
        val resp = okhttp3.OkHttpClient().newCall(req).execute()
        val text = resp.body()?.string().orEmpty()
        withContext(Dispatchers.Main) {
            Toast.makeText(this@MainActivity, text, Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show()
        }
    }
}

Why execute(Params...) is deprecated in API 30+
- Encourages background work tied to Activity lifecycle, causing leaks and crashes on rotation.
- Unclear threading guarantees; parallel vs serial behavior changed across APIs, leading to subtle bugs.
- Modern alternatives (coroutines, WorkManager) provide structured concurrency, cancellation, and lifecycle awareness.

Backward compatibility notes
- Coroutines and OkHttp work back to very old Android versions; they are library-level, not platform APIs, so they’re compatible on API 21+ (and often earlier depending on your minSdk).
- If you must support very old devices, the ExecutorService example works down to API 14+.

Security and best practices when executing remote commands
- Prefer SSH public key auth over passwords; verify the host key (avoid PromiscuousVerifier in production).
- Do not hardcode secrets; use encrypted storage (EncryptedSharedPreferences/Keystore) or fetch securely.
- Restrict commands on the Pi (allowlist actions). Run services with least privilege.
- Use HTTPS/TLS for HTTP approach (reverse proxy like Nginx/Caddy); rate-limit and firewall the port.

How to update your snippet minimally
- Remove AsyncTask usage:

btnUp.setOnClickListener(v -> {
    MainActivity.wifiModuleIp = "192.168.1.100";
    MainActivity.wifiModulePort = 22;
    MainActivity.CMD = "python /path/to/script.py --direction up";

    // Old (deprecated): new Soket_AsyncTask().execute();
    // New (Java):
    exec.submit(() -> {
        try {
            String out = sshExec(MainActivity.wifiModuleIp, MainActivity.wifiModulePort, "pi", "password", MainActivity.CMD);
            runOnUiThread(() -> Toast.makeText(this, "OK: " + out, Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show());
        } catch (Exception e) {
            runOnUiThread(() -> Toast.makeText(this, e.getMessage(), Toast.LENGTH_LONG).show());
        }
    });
});

This preserves your functionality on API 30+ without AsyncTask while offering an HTTP-based alternative if you choose to move away from SSH.
